<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pepoli family</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pepoli were a family of bankers who dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna</a> in the early 14th century. Romeo Pepoli, reputed the richest man in the city, led the commune until his expulsion in 1321, and his son Taddeo Pepoli became lord of Bologna in 1337. Taddeo's sons sold the city to the Visconti of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> in 1350.</p></div>
